92186250829 1111 #uuid "aad0a18b-ba4c-5de3-94dc-4375cd6c03bf" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250830 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250831 13194139533784 true] [17592186250830 1089 "q-165973" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250830 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533784 true] [17592186250830 1100 "What is the range of $y=2(5)^{x}-3?$" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250830 1113 #uuid "3b1c999f-be1d-51d5-bb01-040649089426" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250830 1145 "The range of ${5}^{x}$ is\n\n$$\n{5}^{x}>0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $2$ and then subtracting $3,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{x} & >0 \\\\ 2(5)^{x} & >0 \\\\ 2(5)^{x}-3 & >0-3 \\\\ y & >-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in (-3,\\infty ).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $f(x)=2(5)^{x}-3$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943819/assets/c8179a12c8032d81ebbdb8a5a95c158e905fab4d24aa68f0eeef1f4bc4971a0b.png)" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250832 13194139533784 true] [17592186250831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250833 13194139533784 true] [17592186250831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250834 13194139533784 true] [17592186250831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250835 13194139533784 true] [17592186250831 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250836 13194139533784 true] [17592186250831 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533784 true] [17592186250831 1041 "selection" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250831 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250832 13194139533784 true] [17592186250831 1110 #uuid "b06c741f-03c4-5bc3-b824-7edd41c8c947" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250832 1034 "y\\in (-3,\\infty )" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250832 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533784 true] [17592186250832 1111 #uuid "31939db6-a7a9-5f45-9ab5-1402ddc0c6d3" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250833 1034 "y\\in (-\\infty ,3]" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250833 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533784 true] [17592186250833 1111 #uuid "ea483945-526f-5e91-8b8d-6b294b4384f4" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250834 1034 "y\\in (-\\infty ,-3)" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250834 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533784 true] [17592186250834 1111 #uuid "97c5412c-33e7-5456-bea1-47e85c6cdcb7" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250835 1034 "y\\in [-3,\\infty )" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250835 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533784 true] [17592186250835 1111 #uuid "dbb26809-881f-59cd-9ad7-6ccdbd4919b3" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250836 1034 "y\\in (-\\infty ,3)" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250836 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533784 true] [17592186250836 1111 #uuid "a06172b2-f368-5bf3-9a97-353158d0113b" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250837 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250838 13194139533784 true] [17592186250837 1089 "q-165974" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250837 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533784 true] [17592186250837 1100 "Find the root of $f(x)=2(5)^{x}-50.$" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250837 1113 #uuid "6cd244e5-78b1-5417-9ff1-33275ef2661d" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250837 1145 "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n2(5)^{x}-50=0\n$$\n\nFirst, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by adding $50$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(5)^{x}-50 & =0 \\\\ 2(5)^{x}-\\cancel{50}+\\cancel{50} & =0+50 \\\\ 2(5)^{x} & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing both sides by $2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(5)^{x} & =50 \\\\ {5}^{x} & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite $25$ as ${5}^{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n{5}^{x}={5}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(5)$, we equate the exponents. This gives\n\n$$\nx=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=2.$" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250839 13194139533784 true] [17592186250838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250840 13194139533784 true] [17592186250838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250841 13194139533784 true] [17592186250838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250842 13194139533784 true] [17592186250838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250843 13194139533784 true] [17592186250838 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533784 true] [17592186250838 1041 "selection" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250838 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250839 13194139533784 true] [17592186250838 1110 #uuid "be14988a-21b6-5c88-876b-68312d336e9b" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250839 1034 "2" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533784 true] [17592186250839 1111 #uuid "5f1a89c0-ab2e-514b-836f-d84f77164b61" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250840 1034 "1" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250840 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533784 true] [17592186250840 1111 #uuid "2f88ac03-0a84-5ebc-b718-a4ad34dcf9d1" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250841 1034 "-3" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250841 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533784 true] [17592186250841 1111 #uuid "a59b779a-ac70-560e-915e-b814be89f378" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250842 1034 "-1" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533784 true] [17592186250842 1111 #uuid "d08b65dd-448b-51ae-acb7-b32f88639ef1" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250843 1034 "5" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533784 true] [17592186250843 1111 #uuid "97339d77-57c2-550b-b443-f262fb778acd" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250844 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250845 13194139533784 true] [17592186250844 1089 "q-40392" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250844 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533784 true] [17592186250844 1100 "What is the range of $y=-3(2)^{2-x}-1?$" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250844 1113 #uuid "0ba8974b-b12d-5e2d-8293-45498541a65b" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250844 1145 "The range of ${2}^{-x}$ is \n\n$$\n{2}^{-x}>0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{2}^{2-x}>0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-3$ and then subtracting $1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2-x} & >0 \\\\ -3(2)^{2-x} & <0 \\\\ -3(2)^{2-x}-1 & <0-1 \\\\ y & <-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1).$ \n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $f(x)=-3(2)^{2-x}-1$ is shown below.  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943819/assets/88b75fabc306eb09a7ca63c909de3272cc776bf808e29da4cc08ae2c5a53e192.png)" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250846 13194139533784 true] [17592186250845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250847 13194139533784 true] [17592186250845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250848 13194139533784 true] [17592186250845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250849 13194139533784 true] [17592186250845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250850 13194139533784 true] [17592186250845 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533784 true] [17592186250845 1041 "selection" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250845 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250850 13194139533784 true] [17592186250845 1110 #uuid "91f58415-3af7-5158-bb7c-c3a5e5fdda97" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250846 1034 "y\\in (-\\infty ,1)" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250846 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533784 true] [17592186250846 1111 #uuid "96c36916-a109-55b8-93cd-1751ba74c634" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250847 1034 "y\\in (1,+\\infty )" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250847 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533784 true] [17592186250847 1111 #uuid "0c5c758e-51ba-554f-b5e2-4bd1bd65893b" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250848 1034 "y\\in (-\\infty ,-1]" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250848 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533784 true] [17592186250848 1111 #uuid "6233f435-ecaa-5f75-9856-c9ff32da0583" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250849 1034 "y\\in (-1,+\\infty )" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250849 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533784 true] [17592186250849 1111 #uuid "85c9da1b-b455-561c-848f-9cf1f61b9610" 13194139533784 true] [17592186250850 1034 "y\\in (-\\infty ,-